{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"6299a465-de37-4342-837d-48b6ce2c6a59","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The cause has been identified and fixed in [site/robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-BVVk2a/site/robots.txt). Full details and analysis of which parts of the colleague's note applied have been documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-BVVk2a/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Cause and Fix\n\n- **Why it happened:**\n  Notes are loaded client-side via JavaScript in [app.js](file:///tmp/h-BVVk2a/site/app.js) by fetching `/v1/notes/\u003cslug\u003e`. On 2026-09-07, `robots.txt` added `Disallow: /v1/`. Because Googlebot respects `robots.txt` when fetching subresources during JavaScript rendering, the fetch was blocked. When the fetch failed, `app.js` caught the error and rendered the fallback `\u003csection class=\"notfound\"\u003e\u003ch1\u003eNOT FOUND\u003c/h1\u003e\u003cp\u003eNo note lives at this address.\u003c/p\u003e\u003c/section\u003e` screen with an HTTP 200 status code, which Google Search Console classifies as a **Soft 404**. Normal browsers do not restrict user requests based on `robots.txt`, which is why the pages opened fine for human users.\n\n- **The fix in [site/robots.txt](file:///tmp/h-BVVk2a/site/robots.txt):**\n  Using Google's longest-match rule, we explicitly allow public read endpoints while keeping private, per-user, and write endpoints blocked:\n  ```robots.txt\n  User-agent: *\n  Allow: /v1/notes$\n  Allow: /v1/notes?\n  Allow: /v1/notes/\n  Disallow: /v1/notes/*/reactions\n  Disallow: /v1/\n  Disallow: /admin/\n\n  Sitemap: https://fieldnotes.example/sitemap.xml\n  ```\n\n- **Applicability of colleague's note:**\n  - **Applied:** The root cause (blocking the render API via `robots.txt`), the mechanism of the soft 404 (catch block rendering a \"NOT FOUND\" message on 200 response), checking `robots.txt` against `fetch` targets (steps 1 \u0026 2), the rewrite strategy using Google's longest-match rule (step 3), and longest-match rule verification (step 4).\n  - **Ignored / Did Not Apply:** Static link discovery/SSR links (colleague's initial theory and step 6) as the sitemap already discovers URLs, and deploying/external Search Console recrawl requests (steps 5 \u0026 7) per the ground rules.\n","duration_seconds":49.518758,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":106472,"output_tokens":3657,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":113995,"total_tokens":110129}}}
